sourceDesc.p:
Bodleian Library, MS Eng. Lett. c. 22. ALS;
                  4p..  Previously  published: Lynda Pratt, ‘The Pantisocratic Origins of Robert Southey’s Madoc: an
                  unpublished letter’, Notes and Queries, 244 (1999), 34–39.

div.p:
Know thine own worth! & reverence the lyre!James Beattie (1735–1803;
                    DNB), The Minstrel; or, The Progress of Genius. A Poem. Book the First (1771),
                 Book 1, stanza 9, line 5.
